</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 436)</h2>
<p><b>Loop what you mean — and mark the side you're looking at.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Repeat scope</b> joins the loop style: <b>This Clip</b>, <b>All Clips</b>, or a <b>Range</b> whose in/out (I/O) can cross clip boundaries. The range draws as a yellow band on the sequence strip and saves with the session.</li>
<li><b>⌥L — Loop This Clip</b>: one key loops the clip under the playhead.</li>
<li><b>Marks follow the side you're looking at</b> while comparing, exactly like notes: sketch on the B version and the mark belongs to B — it stays with that version, on its own frames.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
